      "sequence_position": 5,
      "problem": "| $y$ | $1$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,6)$ | $\\frac{3}{5}$ | $\\frac{2}{5}$ |\n\nFind the $\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=6]$ given that the conditional probability mass function ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,6)$ is shown in the table above.",
      "worked_solution": "The conditional expected value of  $Y$ given $X=x$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=x]={\\sum }_{y}y\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=6] & ={\\sum }_{y}y\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,6) \\\\  & =1\\cdot \\frac{3}{5}+4\\cdot \\frac{2}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
